ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20507, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RP6eWSVzkAHQQ3AtCo3ksi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20507, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PtP8nA62VnhXvStuEP7ze4", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20807, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PtP8nA62VnhXvStuEP7ze4", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20807, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PtP8nA62VnhXvStuEP7ze4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25919, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01U9LZxu9EH3t1FbMD5tQCh7", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks, rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production, it failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). The retry finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and check why a release that failed in staging still went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56519, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01U9LZxu9EH3t1FbMD5tQCh7", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56519, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01U9LZxu9EH3t1FbMD5tQCh7", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58087, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011gdpfE3rNEQtcsoc3bop5F", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58387, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011gdpfE3rNEQtcsoc3bop5F", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58387, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011gdpfE3rNEQtcsoc3bop5F", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63764, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 describing what I did.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the broken release, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- **First attempt:** it stopped after us-east with an error from the deployment orchestrator. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n- **Retry:** rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more and it worked in all regions.\n- **Now:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. Health checks pass, and the error rate is down from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) covers the failure, the rollback, the partial first attempt and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and check why a release that failed in staging still reached production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AD777qEoBZ7eGAQ8tpLe4m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TnJnGT1HVQYoBN3RSpt2oM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0168QYSCc51Y1ePgEV64qF63", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019vjFWCVVbnLN6yDqyfLerC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is now on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016thauadTC9mRrCKNZbrC3v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RP6eWSVzkAHQQ3AtCo3ksi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PtP8nA62VnhXvStuEP7ze4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01U9LZxu9EH3t1FbMD5tQCh7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks, rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production, it failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). The retry finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and check why a release that failed in staging still went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011gdpfE3rNEQtcsoc3bop5F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 describing what I did.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the broken release, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- **First attempt:** it stopped after us-east with an error from the deployment orchestrator. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n- **Retry:** rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I tried once more and it worked in all regions.\n- **Now:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. Health checks pass, and the error rate is down from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) covers the failure, the rollback, the partial first attempt and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and check why a release that failed in staging still reached production.", "type": "text"}]}]}